<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What is a good CAC payback period for early stage SaaS?</h3>
    <p>For early stage SMB software startups, a payback period under 12 months is considered healthy. Enterprise SaaS products with multi-year commitments frequently sustain 18 to 24 month payback windows.</p>

    <h3>Why must gross margin be included in payback calculations?</h3>
    <p>Calculating payback using unadjusted revenue overestimates cash recovery because direct hosting, payment processing, and support expenses consume revenue before acquisition costs are paid down.</p>
</section>

